The driver provides support for the 3Com Bluetooth PC Card, model
3CRWB6096,  to  the  Bluetooth  protocol  stack.  This card needs
firmware loaded before it will work. Due  to  copyright  restric‐
tions  we  cannot distribute the firmware with NetBSD, but if you
have the card then you should have received a CD with the drivers
on, or you may download the latest version from the 3Com website.
Create a directory named in the search path of the kernel subsys‐
tem. Now, extract the driver archive and find the  firmware  file
called  and  place  this file in the newly created directory. The
firmware will be loaded automatically as needed.   This  will  be
printed  to  the  console  if the device cannot open the firmware
file as described above.  If the kernel is compiled with the  op‐
tion,  these  messages  will  be produced on the console when the
card antenna position is changed.  These messages  will  be  pro‐
duced  when  the  card is enabled or disabled due to power change
events.  This device driver was written by using and  BlueZ  dri‐
